  "manual": {
    "notes": [
      "MARRIAGE TO 'MARY BLACKMORE' REFUTED (research 2026-07-03): no Larkin x Blackmore marriage exists in England & Wales 1885-1911 (FreeBMD), and the 25 Dec 1905 Ramsgate event belongs to an unrelated Kent bride. Also proven negative: no Thomas Larkin marriage anywhere in Cumberland 1880-1911 — he and his wife married elsewhere (plausibly Ireland, Scotland, or pre-1892 Maine).",
      "Reconciled timeline: b. ~1860-64 Liverpool or Ireland (competing records; the Whitehaven Larkin community was heavily Irish Catholic); 1877 Benedicta/Silver Ridge, Aroostook Co. Maine (an Irish Catholic colony); 1881 transatlantic; by mid-1903 Whitehaven (son Samuel registered Jun Q 1903, 10b/733); possibly widowed Mar Q 1906 (Mary Ellen Larkin, 42, Whitehaven 10b/429 — certificate needed to confirm she was his wife); daughter Ellen born ~Nov 1906; 1911 census Whitehaven; 1914 military; 8 Apr 1918 Howe Brook, Aroostook Co.; d. 1920 Maine, children left in England.",
      "If Mary Ellen (d. Mar 1906) WAS his wife, Ellen's mother was a subsequent, unregistered partner; the GRO mother's-maiden-name lookup on Ellen's registration (10b/689) decides it.",
      "WIFE IDENTIFIED (2026-07-03): Ellen's GRO birth registration gives the mother's maiden name McALONE (record M0001). No Larkin x McAlone marriage registered in Cumberland 1880-1911 — married elsewhere (Ireland/Scotland/pre-1892 Maine plausible)."
    ]
  }
